# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: Demonarc4

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah sat down on the heaped up pile of hay."
    new "Sarah se sentó sobre el montón de paja amontonada."

    old "Outside, the cold winds howled."
    new "Fuera, los vientos helados aullaban."

    old "Sarah could feel the cold wind cut through the gaps and holes of the old ruined castle."
    new "Sarah podía sentir cómo el viento frío atravesaba las grietas y los agujeros del antiguo castillo en ruinas."

    old "Outside was probably worse, but inside was hardly better."
    new "Fuera probablemente era peor, pero adentro apenas iba mejor."

    old "From the corner of her eyes, she watched as Dalia climbed into her bed."
    new "Desde el ángulo de su vista, observó cómo Dalia subía a la cama."

    old "A real bed. An actual bed."
    new "Una cama real. Una cama de verdad."

    old "And instead, she was forced to sit and sleep on a pil of hay, as if she were some farm animal."
    new "Y en su lugar, tuvo que sentarse y dormir sobre un montón de paja, como si fuera algún animal de granja."

    old "A spike of resentment build in her."
    new "Narrador"

    old "What made that girl think she was any better than her?"
    new "¿Qué le hizo pensar a esa chica que era mejor que ella?"

    old "But it faded away just as quickly."
    new "Pero se desvaneció tan rápido."

    old "None of it was Dalia's fault."
    new "Nada de ello era culpa de Dalia."

    old "If anything, this was likely just another game, played on them by the Master."
    new "Si acaso, esto probablemente era solo otro juego, jugado contra ellos por el Maestro."

    old "Pitching them against one another over some trivial thing."
    new "Lanzándolas la una contra la otra por alguna tontería."

    old "Driving a wedge between them."
    new "Introduciendo una cuña entre ellos."

    old "Sarah crawled up into a corner of her hay bed."
    new "Sarah se arrastró hasta una esquina de su cama de paja."

    old "She did her best to make it feel comfortable, knowing that it never would."
    new "Hizo lo mejor que pudo para hacer que se sintiera cómoda, sabiendo que nunca sería así."

    old "Looking over at Dalia, she contemplated asking to join her."
    new "Mirando a Dalia, pensó en pedirle que se uniera a ella."

    old "Simply the idea of her body heat was enough source of comfort."
    new "Simplemente el calor de su cuerpo era suficiente consuelo."

    old "Or the touch of someone that was as close as friend in this wretched place."
    new "O el tacto de alguien que estaba tan cerca como un amigo en este lugar miserable."

    old "But she couldn't ask it."
    new "Pero no podía pedirlo."

    old "Not after everything that had happened today."
    new "No después de todo lo que pasó hoy."

    old "Sarah rolled back to the corner of the hay bed."
    new "Sarah rodó de nuevo hacia la esquina de la cama de paja."

    old "The coarse fabric, stabbing into her skin."
    new "La tela áspera, clavándose en su piel."

    old "She shivered as the cold winds raged through the cracks of the old broken fort."
    new "Temblo mientras los vientos helados aullaban entre las grietas del viejo y derruido fuerte."

    old "Sarah never asked Dalia to join her in the bed."
    new "Sarah nunca pidió a Dalia que se uniera a ella en la cama."

    old "She held out hope that Dalia might invite her instead."
    new "Esperaba que Dalia la invitara en su lugar."

    old "But that hope proved likewise idle."
    new "Pero esa esperanza resultó igualmente vana."

    old "Instead, she slept alone, and had never felt more alone in all her life."
    new "En su lugar, se quedó dormida sola y nunca había sentido tanta soledad en toda su vida."

    old "Sleep with Dalia"
    new "Dormir con Dalia"

    old "Dalia..."
    new "Dalia..."

    old "Would you mind if I...slept in your bed with you?"
    new "¿Te importaría si... dormía en tu cama contigo?"

    old "Sarah watched the girl sit upright."
    new "Sarah observó cómo la chica se sentaba erguida."

    old "Of course!"
    new "¡Por supuesto!"

    old "No reason for you to sleep on that hay. There is plenty of space in the bed for both of us."
    new "No tienes por qué dormir en esa paja. Hay espacio suficiente en la cama para los dos."

    old "Sarah got up and walked towards the bed."
    new "Sarah se levantó y caminó hacia la cama."

    old "Dalia pulled back the covers and Sarah slipped into the bed."
    new "Dalia apartó las sábanas y Sarah se deslizó en la cama."

    old "When Dalia pulled the covers back over the both of them, Sarah instantly felt the warmth."
    new "Cuando Dalia tiró las sábanas para cubrirlos a los dos, Sarah sintió instantáneamente el calor."

    old "Outside, she could still hear the roaring wind, pounding against the frail castle."
    new "Fuera, aún podía oír el viento rugiente golpeando contra el frágil castillo."

    old "But here, underneath the covers, it felt warm. Safe, almost."
    new "Pero aquí, bajo las sábanas, se sentía cálido. Seguro, casi."

    old "Sarah rolled to face Dalia and found the girl already facing her."
    new "Sarah giró para mirar a Dalia y encontró a la chica ya mirándola."

    old "She had been sitting in the dark long enough that her sight had grown used to it."
    new "Había estado sentada en la oscuridad lo suficiente para que su vista se hubiera acostumbrado a ella."

    old "Sarah spoke softly, as if someone might be listening."
    new "Sarah habló con suavidad, como si alguien pudiera estar escuchando."

    old "Perhaps they were."
    new "Quizás lo fueran."

    old "Don't worry."
    new "No te preocupes."

    old "When I first got here, the thing I wanted most of all was someone else here..."
    new "Cuando llegué por primera vez, lo que más deseaba era tener a alguien más aquí..."

    old "You wanted someone else to be in this hell?"
    new "¿Querías a alguien más en este infierno?"

    old "No, not literally. But just the idea...that I would have someone that I could be with."
    new "No, no literalmente. Pero solo la idea... de tener a alguien con quien estar."

    old "Someone other than Him."
    new "Alguien más que Él."

    old "I understand. I'm also happy that I'm not alone."
    new "Entiendo. También estoy contenta de no estar sola."

    old "That much was the truth."
    new "Eso era la verdad."

    old "Thank you, by the way."
    new "Por cierto, gracias."

    old "For what?"
    new "¿Para qué?"

    old "For not fighting the Master."
    new "Por no luchar contra el Maestro."

    old "I mean...I know it's not easy..."
    new "Bueno... sé que no es fácil..."

    old "Sarah reached out and touched Dalia."
    new "Sarah se estiró y tocó a Dalia."

    old "With the tip of her fingers, she felt her naked skin."
    new "Con la punta de sus dedos, sintió su piel desnuda."

    old "Dalia was wearing her outfit, but she might as well be nude."
    new "Dalia llevaba puesto su atuendo, pero podría pasar por desnuda."

    old "When I heard he would punish you if I defied him, I knew I wouldn't let that happen."
    new "Cuando supe que te castigaría si lo desafiaba, sabía que no dejaría que eso ocurriera."

    old "Taking the punishment myself is one thing, but I couldn't make you suffer like that."
    new "Asumir el castigo yo misma es una cosa, pero no podía hacerte sufrir de esa manera."

    old "Thank you. You really are a good friend."
    new "Gracias. Eres realmente una buena amiga."

    old "Friend. Was that what they were."
    new "Amigo. ¿Eso era lo que eran."

    old "Some part of her wanted to desperately trust this girl. Some other part of her warned her against it."
    new "Algunas partes de ella deseaban desesperadamente confiar en esta chica, mientras que otras la advertían contra ello."

    old "But in the midst of all that loneliness, it was a tempting idea. A friend."
    new "Pero en medio de toda esa soledad, fue una idea tentadora. Un amigo."

    old "Now, let's try to get some sleep."
    new "Ahora, intentemos dormir un poco."

    old "Another long day tomorrow."
    new "Otro largo día mañana."

    old "Sarah softly nodded, and before long, the two of them were fast asleep."
    new "Sarah asintió suavemente y, antes de que lo supieran, los dos ya estaban profundamente dormidos."
